  "rules": {
    "seller_price_pack_normalization_scope_v1": "The five seller pages freeze offer assertions rather than current delivered prices or taste results. DOVE SKU B07L9TTQN6 is 25.45 dollars with no reviews shown and its title and quick look say twelve 3.30-ounce dark bars. Lindt SKU B000H26J7E is 30 dollars, rated 67 percent over twelve reviews, with the selected 70-percent 3.5-ounce twelve-pack. Ritter Sport SKU B07PTSPCVS is 8.99 dollars with no reviews shown for one 74-percent 100-gram or 3.52-ounce bar. Green & Black SKU B008FRKKV4 is 21.99 dollars with no reviews shown for three 70-percent 100-gram bars. Raaka SKU B07811Q1PR is 14.95 dollars, rated 58 percent over twelve reviews, with a selected coconut-milk 60-percent 1.8-ounce three-pack; its title implies 5.4 ounces while Product Dimensions reports 1.8 ounces. Conditional arithmetic from the title fields gives about 2.12, 2.50, 8.99, 7.33 and 4.98 dollars per nominal bar respectively, but only after preserving pack and mass assumptions, and none is a verified current delivered cost or taste ranking.",
    "comparable_form_price_ladder_boundary_v1": "A causal price ladder requires like-for-like products and portions. The DOVE page does not state a cocoa percentage in the captured text; Lindt and Green & Black say 70 percent, Ritter says 74 percent, and Raaka says 60 percent with coconut milk, shredded coconut and unroasted cacao. Pack count, bar mass, recipe, percentage, origin and flavor differ. Normalize transparent price fields, but first screen plain dark bars into a comparable stratum and analyze flavored or coconut-containing bars separately. A higher price per bar, per ounce or per 100 grams cannot by itself prove ingredient quality, flavor complexity, preference or health benefit.",
    "process_ethics_label_boundary_v1": "Bean-to-bar describes control from procuring cocoa beans to producing the finished chocolate and can involve processing whole beans rather than remelting an existing base. Fair trade cocoa is defined as cocoa under a certified price-support scheme intended to support sustainable farmer income. Raaka's unroasted, bean-to-bar, small-batch, single-origin, organic, direct-source and beyond-fair-trade statements remain seller assertions for that exact page. Neither the general definitions nor the seller copy guarantee blind taste superiority, complete traceability, exact payments, universal ethical superiority, health benefit or value for this buyer.",
    "cocoa_composition_quality_boundary_v1": "Dry cocoa solids are the components left after cocoa butter is extracted, while some legal uses of cocoa solids include cocoa mass, powder and butter; a percentage label therefore does not alone reveal the balance of non-fat solids, cocoa butter, sugar or every ingredient. Bulk cocoa is contrasted with flavor cocoa using a partly subjective definition that refers to undesirable flavor, drying or fermentation, while the same page notes grade and origin variation. Percentage, bean class, origin and processing can be variables to bind and test, but generic pages do not grade any captured bar or establish a monotonic price-to-quality curve.",
    "community_habit_value_scope_v1": "One author reports eating a bar or two daily while trying to cut down. A second author reports sending six roughly three-ounce dark bars of various types as a gift before an unrelated dog-ingestion incident. A Pittsburgh author lists Aldi favorites because of price and quality and includes chocolate-flavored ice cream, not a controlled dark-bar comparison. These pages motivate recording use frequency, trying small varied units and separating price from personal quality, but they do not supply population consumption guidance, safety advice, brand rankings, blind preferences or a universal value threshold.",
    "blinded_difference_liking_protocol_v1": "Sensory analysis separates analytical testing of whether products differ from affective testing of which product is liked. A hedonic scale records degree of liking, commonly from one to nine, while a blinded experiment withholds information that could influence participants or investigators. For the buyer's question, verify exact labels and allergens, select comparable plain bars, serve equal coded portions in randomized balanced order, repeat sessions, record whether a difference is detected separately from nine-point liking and purchase willingness, and record guesses or other unblinding. Seller identity, package and price stay hidden until scoring is locked. This single-person protocol estimates only this buyer's repeatable preference under declared conditions.",
    "person_specific_price_stop_rule_v1": "Before tasting, declare the smallest liking improvement worth paying for, the maximum incremental cost per evening, the number of repeated sessions, a consistency rule and identity, allergen, package and sensory stops. After current delivered prices and portions are verified, move through comparable tiers only while the next tier produces the declared repeatable difference and liking gain without exceeding the cost ceiling. The first tier that fails that compound rule is a person-specific stopping point under the tested products and conditions, not a universal market breakpoint. If no premium clears it, keep the lower-cost bar; if fields or comparability remain unresolved, run a smaller corrected trial or defer.",
    "price_ladder_decision_preparation_v1": "Build one exact-offer table with literal seller fields, transparent conditional arithmetic, comparable-form status, label and allergen completeness, process and ethics claim status, and current delivered-price verification. Then add blinded difference, nine-point liking, repeatability, incremental evening cost and willingness-to-pay results. Do not let marketing, cocoa percentage, ratings, anecdotes or an ethics priority substitute for the sensory and budget gates, and do not let a sensory win erase unresolved identity or allergen fields. Preserve an ethics preference as its own declared decision axis rather than calling it a measured taste improvement.",
    "evidence_bounded_price_ladder_decision_v1": "The packet proves no universal point at which dark-chocolate price stops improving quality and no immediate winner. Audit the frozen offers and their pack and mass assumptions; separate comparable plain bars from the Raaka coconut recipe; keep bean-to-bar and Fairtrade at process and ethics scope; and run the predeclared randomized blinded repeated protocol with distinct difference, liking and cost outcomes. Choose the lowest-cost exact comparable bar that clears identity, allergen, repeatable sensory and budget gates. Otherwise keep the current bar, run a smaller corrected trial or defer. Report any stopping point only for this buyer, these verified bars, prices, portions and test conditions."
